# Top-level packages of the tools layer (debug, trace, profile, benchmark, pressure, filesystem and
# image tools, QEMU, libvirt, Docker). Everything else in the layer is their dependency closure,
# resolved against the development image and pinned with checksums in tools.lock.
# Left out on purpose, because the development image already provides them: gcc, binutils, make,
# rustc, cargo, and busybox's tar, gzip, unzip, cpio, xxd, od, hexdump, fdisk, mkfs.vfat, fallocate,
# truncate, nsenter, unshare, ionice, setpriv, timeout, nc. Where busybox only has a reduced applet,
# the real tool below takes over its path (apk installs it over the busybox link).
#
# C/C++ build, format, lint, static analysis
#   g++ libstdc++-dev     C++ compiler and standard library (the dev layer has the C compiler only)
#   linux-headers         kernel UAPI headers (ptrace, perf_event, bpf, netlink, loop, ... programs)
#   pkgconf               pkg-config for C/C++ projects and cargo build scripts
#   cmake samurai         CMake and the ninja-compatible builder
#   file                  identify binaries (ELF type, stripped, linkage)
#   clang22               clang/clang++ (links with the gcc toolchain of the dev layer)
#   compiler-rt           clang's runtime libraries: ASan, UBSan, TSan, LSan, MSan, coverage and profile instrumentation
#   clang22-extra-tools   clang-format, clang-tidy
#   cppcheck              static analysis independent of the compiler
# Rust format, lint, test, profile
#   rustfmt rust-clippy   cargo fmt, cargo clippy
#   rust-gdb              gdb wrapper with the Rust pretty printers
#   cargo-nextest         test runner
#   cargo-flamegraph      cargo flamegraph (perf + flamegraph)
# Debug, trace, profile
#   gdb strace ltrace valgrind
#   perf                  perf record/report/stat/bench/trace (software events only in a VM)
#   bpftool               inspect and load eBPF programs and maps
# Benchmark
#   hyperfine             command-line benchmarking
#   sysbench              CPU, memory, file I/O, threads, mutex
#   fio                   block and file I/O
#   benchmark benchmark-dev   Google Benchmark library, for C++ micro-benchmarks
# Resource pressure
#   stress-ng             CPU, memory, process, thread, file descriptor, I/O, network (socket) stressors
#   iperf3                TCP/UDP throughput
#   iproute2              ip, ss, tc, bridge (the busybox ip is reduced)
#   tcpdump               packet capture
#   lsof                  open files per process (the busybox lsof ignores its arguments)
# Filesystem and disk image creation and inspection
#   e2fsprogs e2fsprogs-extra   mke2fs -d, e2fsck, debugfs, resize2fs, tune2fs, dumpe2fs, e2image
#   fuse2fs               ext2/3/4 image access over FUSE without a kernel mount
#   dosfstools mtools     FAT: mkfs.fat, fsck.fat, mcopy, mdir
#   squashfs-tools        mksquashfs, unsquashfs
#   erofs-utils           mkfs.erofs, dump.erofs, fsck.erofs
#   xfsprogs              mkfs.xfs, xfs_db, xfs_repair
#   btrfs-progs           mkfs.btrfs --rootdir, btrfs inspect-internal
#   xorriso               ISO 9660 images
#   qemu-img              qcow2/raw/vmdk conversion, info, check, snapshots
#   util-linux-misc losetup partx sfdisk gptfdisk blkid lsblk findmnt mount umount wipefs
#                         the real util-linux tools (taskset, chrt, prlimit, nsenter, ...) next to busybox's
# Virtual machines (QEMU TCG without /dev/kvm; KVM where the cloud environment provides it)
#   qemu-system-x86_64 seabios ovmf   emulator, BIOS, UEFI firmware
#   libvirt-daemon libvirt-client libvirt-qemu   libvirtd, virsh, the QEMU driver
# Containers
#   docker-engine docker-cli docker-cli-compose docker-cli-buildx
#   containerd runc       container runtime stack under dockerd
#   iptables nftables     dockerd and libvirt networking
